WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
>>>>>

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.350
KISS! KISS! I’m in love.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.620
This never-ending LOOP,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.840
a cycle that goes out of spin,

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.270
and runs towards you.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.740
Under this bright sunlight,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.040
and blue sky,

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.540
I’m accelerating so fast that I can’t stop moving.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.690
It’s my first time having these feelings.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.450
What should I do? My throbbing heart doesn’t know,

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:46.590
and keeps searching for the solution, even now.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.720
KISS! KISS! I’m in love.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.400
I am here because of your kiss,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.350
which has stopped the flow of time.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.870
I knock on the door to your heart,

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.870
and watch your wavering dreams.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.640
Your RUBY eyes are what absorb me in.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.550
Barely in sight,

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:15.880
the translucent door to your heart looks like it is opening now.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.400
Only you...

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.830
my kiss will reach...

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.060
Would you like to go out with me?

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.350
Eh?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.440
Does that mean...

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.770
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.030
Sorry, did you wait long?

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.080
Shall we go now?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.540
Okay.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.290
Kai-kun!

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.290
Hold on!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.630
Hey, Kai-kun, hey!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:27.810
I think you could at least tell me where I'm being taken to.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.140
You'll know when we get there.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.120
Hey is this place...

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.740
So, it was a live jazz show?!

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.320
What was that?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.390
He's a regular at the store I work at.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.400
The person that was playing the sax?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.610
His phrasing is really extraordinary.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.900
He sometimes lets me see his gigs so I can learn from him.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.360
How was it?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.360
Truthfully, I don't know.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.490
It was pretty amazing though.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.870
That's how it always is the first time.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.120
What do you listen to, Mizusawa?

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:17.920
Music wise?

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.130
Let's see...

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:25.510
Usually western stuff, but I like the oldies too, like Billy Joel.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.260
"Just the Way You Are."

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.430
I love that song!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.930
There's a sax in that song too, if I recall.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.680
It's Phil Woods.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.600
Eh?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:35.890
That sax,

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.100
he's one of my favorite jazz musicians.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.980
I see,

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.740
hey, don't you perform live, Kai-kun?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.740
I'm still not good enough.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.030
That's not true,

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.990
you were really something else when you were practicing by yourself.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.140
I'm the happiest when I spend my time with you like this.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.400
I'm going to stop being halfhearted.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:22.900
Let's get married!

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:26.030
Nijou!

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:43.380
Don't you regret doing all of this so halfheartedly?!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.590
Just mind your own business!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.010
What's wrong, onii-chan?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.430
You've been spacing out this whole time.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.020
I-It's nothing,

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.890
I was just watching "Harusuna."

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:01.400
Could it be you were thinking about Sakino-senpai?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.100
Eh?

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.190
I knew it!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.230
You're wrong!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.110
I wasn't thinking about her like that!

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.320
Hey, is it true onii-chan?

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.200
Are you going out with Sakino-senpai, after all?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.030
Are you, are you?!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.160
I told you I'm not!

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.120
What is it?!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.120
Shut up!

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.620
Besides, it doesn't concer-

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.790
It doesn't concern you.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.970
Fine,

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.340
I'll watch "Harusuna" with Iwao-kun!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.560
Hey, Mao-neechan.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:43.900
Yeah?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.110
Where did you go today?

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:48.900
Why?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.700
No, how do I say it,

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.950
I just thought you were more dressed up than usual.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.950
Could it have been a date?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.040
Did you find someone you like?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.830
Why? Are you worried?

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.830
N-Not really.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.170
And, how about you?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.130
W-What?

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:07.960
Don't play dumb.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.510
Did you make some progress with Yuumi-chan?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:11.050
Eh?

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.590
Ah, no.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.470
Hey, wait, don't leave me behind!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.060
Even if you say that!

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.020
Just you wait I'll be the one to leave you behind!

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.700
Be brave, Kouichi, Kazuki!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.410
You'll be fine, you can jump, you can jump!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.580
Come on!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.050
Jump over here!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.510
Come on, hurry up!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.390
You're a boy, aren't you, Kouichi?!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.270
Kouichi!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:16.200
Iwao-sama, you're as lovely as boiling udon this morning!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:21.490
Juliet, you're as beautiful as adorned noodles!

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.830
My, my, Iwao-sama, your flattery is quite skillful!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.000
What are you saying, Juliet?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.540
Among all the women in the world,

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.000
there are none as beautiful as you!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.090
I love you the most in the entire world!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.050
We're almost at school, you two.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.930
Iwao-sama!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.050
Juliet!

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.930
Put those away before Kuryuu-san finds them.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.180
Morning, Kazuki!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.180
Morning!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.480
Good morning, Mao-neechan!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.980
Good morning, Mizusawa-senpai!

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.570
You're looking well this morning, Mao-neechan.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.320
After seeing these two faces, my low blood pressure just vanished.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.660
What about you, Kazuki?

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:02.660
Eh?

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.870
You've been looking restless.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.210
R-Really?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.670
I don't think I've been like that, though.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.800
Yesterday, onii-chan and I...

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.880
Did you have a fight or something?

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.550
It wasn't that bad.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.300
Anyway, it's nothing.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.810
Morning, Kai-kun!

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.150
Y-Yeah.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.570
Thanks for yesterday.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.870
So, how's it going?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:44.870
Huh?

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:45.790
How's what going?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.910
The screenplay for the movie.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.540
I'm asking if you've made any progress.

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.040
Have you written the synopsis yet?

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.050
You have the foundation for the plot, at the least, right?

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.220
You leave things to people, and now you've become quite bossy, eh?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.100
The screenplay is the life of a movie!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.600
A lot of pioneers have said to put priority on the screenplay,

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.560
above all others in a production, haven't they?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.480
So, how is it?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.860
A-Ah, yeah...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.450
A love story?

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:22.570
Yes.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:27.450
Sorry, I don't often see movies.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.660
All the movies I've seen have mostly been...

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.630
Well, I guess.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.050
Generally, movies tend to have love involved somehow.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.340
Also, a Russian writer said that stories are born,

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:44.510
because there is unrequited love in this world.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.930
U-Unrequited?!

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.100
Eh?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.310
No, I didn't mean that!

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.860
Maybe you should do that!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.030
Perhaps the bear and gorilla,

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.940
Gyouza and Wantan, should have a role.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:04.070
T-They don't, they don't need a role!

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.410
Thank you, Hoshino-san.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.620
I think a love story will be great.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.630
I think I'm able to see the direction it's going in.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.430
Oh, really?

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:27.100
Let me hear it right away, then.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:30.930
And the chocolate cake there was really good!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.140
The store's uniform is really cute too!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.190
Hey, let's all go together next time!

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.610
Chocolate cake, huh?

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:37.860
Sounds good!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:38.770
Let's go!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.860
Yeah, let's go!

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.080
A love story, huh?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:57.920
I see.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.380
I think it's reasonable, coming from you, Sanada.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:06.180
You say it's a love story, but there are many variations:

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.220
fated love,

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.850
forbidden love,

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:10.970
mistaken love.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.890
There are many types of love in the world.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.980
Hey, there's space over there.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.320
It's Futami-san.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.740
Reckless love.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.660
I-It's not that.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.950
It's quite unusual for Futami-san to come to the cafeteria.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.710
What's wrong?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.250
This is a perfect chance to get closer to the girl genius.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.720
What's with the deplorable look?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.640
You're like a son who went through a time-slip,

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.720
to learn the basics of love from his father-in-law.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.350
I told you, it's not like that!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.890
Hey, Aihara!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.790
She didn't even invite me today.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.120
So, this is where you were.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.460
Mao-neechan!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.250
What's with the gloomy look?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.630
You wouldn't feel that down from a fight with Nana-chan, right?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.850
Do you want to tell me what happened?

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.770
Do you remember, Mao-neechan?

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.110
Remember what?

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:47.900
The swings.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.490
Huh?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.910
When we were small, we played at the park,

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.990
and you jumped off of the swings.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.620
Did that happen?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.250
It was so cool,

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.670
that Kouichi and I said, "Amazing!"

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.010
Kouichi jumped too.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:14.350
We tried to copy you, and were so scared that we couldn't really jump.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.640
That Kouichi...

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.600
But, I...

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.360
Be brave, Kazuki!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.360
Come on!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.030
It'll be fine, Kouichi did it too!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.580
You can jump too, Kazuki!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.710
Come on, hurry up!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.840
Come on, Kazuki!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.430
You're a boy, aren't you, Kazuki?

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.300
Kazuki!

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.940
I remember now!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:08.190
Out of the three of us, you jumped the furthest, Kazuki!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:08.650
Eh?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:09.780
I did?

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:13.280
What, you brought it up and you forgot?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:18.370
You were kind of crying and looked desperate, but then you jumped!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.870
We tried to dodge you.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.330
That jump was really amazing.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.330
It's really nostalgic.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.500
So, what about that story?

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:33.220
Kazuki?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.720
We shall be afraid of experience,

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:44.190
which is the best of all teachers.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:49.650
And at the end, we shall find that we have profited nothing,

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:53.240
by all the dangers we have avoided.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.110
Try translating this.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.120
Um...

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:00.740
Kai!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.330
What's wrong? Hurry up and translate it.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.750
I'm sorry, I wasn't listening.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:10.920
I thought so.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.380
So were you listening to that again?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.380
The music playing in your head?

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.550
Not going to a university and going down the path of music.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.680
How splendid.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.520
It's great to look at dreams,

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:29.440
but to ascertain your abilities, you should learn to study.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.900
Well then, Tachibana, you translate it.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.440
Yes.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.870
Want to go home together, Sanada?

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.200
Eh?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.160
You were able to decide the direction the movie is taking.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.670
Let's go to a cafe or something and brainstorm.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:53.420
Ah, sorry, but I have some things to take care of.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:54.420
Later.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:55.630
Hey!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.430
Can't be helped then, Aihara!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:19.820
Are you going to work now?

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.660
Let me hear you perform.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.330
You promised that you'd let me hear you play sometime, right?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:42.010
Ah, Iwao-sama, how I've longed to see you again!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.010
And I as well, Juliet!

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:50.480
It felt like I waited many times over the time it takes to boil udon!

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.940
Iwao-sama!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.150
Juliet!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.400
I'm going to stop being halfhearted.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:58.950
Let's get married!

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:02.120
Oh, Iwao-sama!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:23.890
This is...

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:28.520
I thought they might be helpful for thinking of ideas for a story.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.770
"The Sorrows of Young Werther."

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:32.940
It's a classic.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:37.320
The lead character, who fell in love with a lady who has a fiancé,

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.740
was at a loss of what to do, that he committed suicide with a pistol.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:42.860
"Kokoro."

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.570
That's by Natsumi Souseki.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:50.000
The lead character stole his best friend's lover, causing his friend to commit suicide,

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.250
then, he is tormented by his parent's torture for many years, and later commits suicide himself.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.460
"The Apple Tree."

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.170
I like that one!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.430
With his wedding nearing, the lead character tries to elope with his lover.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:06.640
He is then charmed by another woman and leaves his lover.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:12.390
The one left behind was drowning in sadness... And committed suicide at... A memorable place.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.900
I-I'm so sorry!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.990
I never realized how inclined I was.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.910
Ah, no.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:30.120
Stories are born because there is unrequited love in this world, right?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.460
But, let's go with a more upbeat feeling this time.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.170
O-Okay.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.760
Be brave, Kazuki!

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:46.050
Come on!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:50.310
It'll be fine, Kouichi did it too!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.560
You can jump too, Kazuki!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.690
Come on, hurry up!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:54.770
Come on, Kazuki!

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.440
You're a boy, aren't you, Kazuki?

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:12.580
F-Fu-Futami-san!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:19.090
U-U-U-Um...

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.390
Let's resume the experiment!

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.980
kowaresou de

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.980
It looks like it’s about to fall apart.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.940
taisetsu sugite sawarenakatta

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.940
So precious that I couldn’t touch it.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.650
wasarenai yo

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.650
I won’t forget

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:47.410
hoshi ni negai o

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:47.410
that wish upon a star.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:22:00.130
kyou shitsu no sumi ni wa itsumo fushigi bako

00:21:55.620 --> 00:22:00.130
The strange box lying in the corner of the classroom;

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:02.500
dare ni mo misenai shi

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:02.500
I won’t show it to anyone.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.300
itsumo minai furi

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.300
I always pretend not to see it.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:11.220
hajimete okutte moratta hoshi no yoru

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:11.220
The first time you walked me home during that starry night.

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:13.600
ano kajitsu mo

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:13.600
The fruit

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:16.180
mada tabetenai kedo

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:16.180
I have not eaten.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:19.020
honki de butsukatta

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:19.020
I struck it with all my might.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.810
naite sawaida

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.810
I cried and I screamed.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:30.320
shinkei wa kitto kinui totokoutetsu de dekiteta

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:30.320
I’m certain nerves are made from silk and steel.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.950
osaekirenai

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.950
My insuppressible feelings

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:36.960
omoi o nagete negai boshi ni

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:36.960
are cast on a wishing star.

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.580
ima kakeru yo

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.580
It’s now time to run.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:42.000
tobira no soto wa DAIAMONDO

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:42.000
Beyond the door are diamonds.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:47.970
ikusen no yume kaki utsushita NOOTO ni

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:47.970
Thousands of dreams transcribed onto a notebook.

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:53.050
tojikometara ai ni yuku yo

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:53.050
Whenever I’m trapped I’m go see you.

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:59.020
kirakira toeien o kiritotta mamade

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:59.020
The sparkle and eternity are cut short.

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:03.980
yakusoku shita kimi to nara ano hi no KISU o

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:03.980
We made a promise with a kiss on that day.

